--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [namespace.udecl]/19: `using B::operator int;' in the public part of A
makes the conversion function a public member of A, although B is a private
base.  The front end reported "member 'B::operator(signed_int)($constthis)'
is not accessible (private)" (bin53): the using-declaration did not adjust
the conversion function's access as it does for other members.
test_overloads.desc: [class.access.general]/5, access is checked after
overload resolution -- the private B::operator char is a candidate that
was diagnosed although operator int is selected.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18
accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
